/**
 * PUMA admin left sidebar (MIT, Tiger-original).
 *
 * The collapsible nav rail. Renders the menu partial in the SAME scope (render())
 * so $this->nav flows through. Collapse/off-canvas behavior is in tiger.prefs.js
 * (toggled via the header's data-tiger-toggle="sidebar" button).
 *
 * The SITE block is the way OUT of admin to the public site — deliberately above the nav and
 * NOT a registered Tiger_Admin_Nav item, so it can't be reordered, ACL-filtered, or pushed down
 * the list by a module. It reuses `.tiger-nav` for styling but omits `data-nav-group`, which is
 * what tiger.admin-nav.js binds to — so it gets the look without joining the collapsible groups.
 */
